<title>CHINA: China's Tarim Jan crude oil output 345,900 T.</title>
<headline>China's Tarim Jan crude oil output 345,900 T.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tarim oilfield in China's northwestern Xinjiang region produced 345,900 tonnes of crude oil in January, the China Petroleum News said on Monday.</p>
<p>The oilfield aims to produce more than 4.0 million tonnes of crude oil in 1997, it said. Oil officials have said its oil output was likely to hit 4.4 million tonnes.</p>
<p>A new oilfield in the Tarim basin, the Tazhongsi oilfield with annual capacity of 2.0 million tonnes, is expected to start production in the first half, it said, but gave no further details.</p>
</text>
